        client:load
      /></InstrumentBand
    >
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2 id="03">03 / Implementation assessment</h2>
    <p>
      The accepted appearance and interaction are recorded here and in the
      retained Flight instrument. Practice has not adopted them. Its existing
      production renderer and simulation remain unchanged; the atmosphere,
      sunlight, cloud and heat painters belong to this study instrument. A prior
      integration attempt modified shared rock lighting and production passes,
      introduced regressions, and has been removed.
    </p>
    <p>
      The accepted boundary is ship-hull overlap. Production behavior, when
      implemented, should use that same overlap for visible entry, damage, drag
      and heat activation. The intended rates are 1 hull/s in the outer 30% and
      2 hull/s deeper inside, integrated with simulation time and normal hull
      lifecycle. Exact classification at the 30% boundary is not a design
      requirement.
    </p>
    <p>
      The implementation attempt was not retained as a production baseline. This
      study remains available for integration comparison; any future work must
      be checked against the established renderer and other active workspace
      changes before adoption.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2 id="04">04 / Impact as Practice’s placeholder Earth</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>No design-principle change is proposed.</strong>
      The accepted production scope below remains pending. This record closes
      design exploration while retaining the instrument as an integration
      reference.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Shared appearance and Practice body — pending.</strong>
        Promote the accepted rock/cloud/rim composition only through established
        renderer owners. Define any new data contract with Zod before consumers.
        Add Impact as placeholder Earth to Practice and its canonical preview
        while preserving the existing bodies and loading fallback.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Atmospheric gameplay — pending.</strong>
        Add the accepted hull-overlap damage rates and modest,
        direction-preserving drag to production simulation. Keep existing
        gravity, solid contact and death behavior intact. Verify outside,
        shallow, boundary, deep, exit, reset, pause, fatal damage and equal
        simulated time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Heat cue and integration — pending.</strong>
        Integrate the accepted curved band and soft LFX glow with actual overlap
        and planet-relative motion through established FX ownership. Preserve
        the shared FX lifecycle and verify entry, fading exit, replay/wrap,
        production scales and keyboard/touch play.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Earth geography, habitation, new cloud materials, differential cloud
      rotation, temperature accumulation and further planet taxonomy remain out
      of scope. Earlier Earth studies remain stopped; this accepted placeholder
      satisfies the immediate Practice need without retroactively accepting
      their rejected designs. Further Earth exploration is deferred.
    </p>
  </section>
